  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Dry, with temperatures trending above normal \nthrough the end of the week\n\nSurface high pressure and a mid-level ridge have started to \nbuild in, bringing a warmer and drier airmass to southern New \nEngland. This will enhance the warming trend throughout the \nweek, allowing temperatures to climb into the low 70s today, mid\nto upper 70s by Thursday, and near 80 by Friday. Despite the \nhigh pressure, lingering low-level moisture from the previous \nweekend's nor'easter will lead to quite a bit of cloud cover \nover the next few days.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Next chance for showers arrives Friday with a \nsweeping cold front followed by a sharp drop in temperatures.\n\nThe next round of showers arrives sometime Friday as a low \npressure system moves across Ontario and Quebec Thursday and \nFriday and a trailing cold front sweeps through New England \nFriday. Some uncertainty still remains on the exact timing of \nwhen the front will pass, but latest guidance has honed in on \nthe evening/overnight hours into Saturday morning. Regardless, \nnot expecting much QPF out of this... less than a quarter inch \nlikely. Most guidance is showing the front stalling out \nsomewhere south of our waters, \n\nOnce the low moves through Quebec, a rather strong continental \nhigh pressure system will build over Ontario, sinking those +4C \nto +6C 850mb temperatures down into New England and sharply \ndropping surface temperatures through the weekend... overnight \ntemps likely drop into the upper 30s to low 40s and daytime \nhighs in the mid 60s.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 3...A secondary, sharp temperature drop is expected\nwith potential for more showers heading into next week.\n\nTowards the second half of the weekend and into early next \nweek, ensemble guidance is suggesting the potential for a \ndeepening low to sweep across the James Bay, possibly bringing \nanother round of shower to southern New England heading into \nMonday morning. A strong high pressure system builds in right on\nthe heels of the low, bringing a secondary shot of even colder \nair to New England. 850mb temperatures could drop to near or \njust below 0C by Tuesday, supporting surface highs in low 50s \nwith nighttime lows possibly falling into the 30s.",
